Wait, is `@angular/router/testing` available? Yes, RouterTestingModule from @angular/router/testing is standard in Angular. package.json has @angular/router.

Actually, hold on — my new spec test queries `fixture.nativeElement.querySelectorAll('mat-menu mat-menu-item')` — the mat-menu content is rendered inside a portal/overlay, not in the DOM until opened. `mat-menu-item` buttons are rendered inside the overlay which may not be attached. Actually the MatMenu content is in an overlay container added to the body, and it's only attached after the menu is opened. So menuItems.length would be 0. That test would be flaky/wrong.

Let me simplify the test to just check the account_circle icon and the presence of the matMenuTriggerFor button. Let me fix the spec to be robust:

```ts
it('should display the account menu when showProfile is true', () => {
  component.showProfile = true;
  fixture.detectChanges();

  const icon = fixture.nativeElement.querySelector('mat-icon');
  expect(icon).toBeTruthy();
  expect(icon.textContent.trim()).toBe('account_circle');
  expect(fixture.nativeElement.querySelector('.user-name')).toBeTruthy();
});
```

Actually `mat-icon` textContent — with a mat-icon, the glyph ligature text is in textContent. That works in tests. Let me simplify. Also the `*ngIf="showProfile"` means when false, no mat-icon. So the test sets showProfile true.

Let me rewrite the spec more simply.

